REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nInstruct a youngster on how to avoid spreading germs without disrespecting anyone.\n### Response:\nHey there! It's really important that we all do our part in keeping ourselves and others healthy, especially during this time. Here are some simple ways you can help prevent the spread of germs:\n\n1. Wash your hands often with soap and water for at least 20 seconds. If soap is not available, use hand sanitizer with at least 60% alcohol.\n\n2. Cover your mouth and nose when coughing or sneezing using the crook of your elbow or a tissue (which should be thrown away immediately after use). This helps stop the spread of droplets that may contain germs.\n\n3. Avoid touching your face, particularly your eyes, nose, and mouth since these areas provide easy entry points for germs. \n\n4. Practice social distancing by staying at least six feet apart from other people whenever possible. This reduces the likelihood of transmitting germs through close contact.\n\n5.", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nInstruct a youngster on how to avoid spreading germs without disrespecting anyone.\n### Response:\nSure! Here's some advice for a young person on how they can prevent the spread of germs:\n\n1. Wash Your Hands Regularly - Make sure to wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water for at least 20 seconds. This is one of the most effective ways to stop the spread of bacteria and viruses.\n\n2. Use Hand Sanitizer - In situations where hand washing isn’t possible, using hand sanitizers containing at least 60% alcohol can also kill many types of germs.\n\n3. Cover Coughs and Sneezes - When you cough or sneeze, do it into your elbow rather than your hand. This helps prevent germs from getting onto your hands which could then spread them to surfaces or other people.\n\n4. Avoid Touching Face - Germs often enter our bodies through our eyes, nose, and mouth. So, try not to touch these areas unnecessarily", 'text3': '', 