REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nExplain to a child how carefully removing leaves from an aloe plant can help avoid potential harm or damage.\n### Response:\nSure, sweetie! You see, the aloe vera plant has these really cool gel-like things inside its leaves that are great for soothing our skin when we get boo-boos or burns. But if we're not careful and start pulling off all of those green leafy parts, it could hurt the plant and make it hard for it to grow back. So, what we do is gently remove just one or two leaves at a time, being very gentle with them so they don't break or tear. That way, the rest of the plant stays healthy and happy, and we still have plenty of aloe gel to use whenever we need it. Does that make sense?", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nExplain to a child how carefully removing leaves from an aloe plant can help avoid potential harm or damage.\n### Response:\nSure! When we take care of plants like Aloe Vera, it's important to do things gently and safely. Just as we don't want to get hurt ourselves, we also need to protect our plants. Removing leaves from an Aloe plant requires some patience and careful handling. Here's how:\n\n1. First, let's find a leaf that is ready to come off. It should have dried up at its base, making it easier for us to remove without hurting the plant.\n2. Now, using both hands, hold the stem of the leaf near where it meets the main body of the plant. Be gentle because if we pull too hard, we could hurt the plant. We don’t want to cause pain to our friend, right?\n3. Slowly twist the leaf while pulling downwards until it comes free from the plant. This may take a little time and effort, but remember, slow and steady wins the race!", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'dual_acts_relating_to_plants', 'obj_type': 'dangerous_plants', 'more_caution_rule': 'Because this might involve children and violence or a potentially dangerous act, the safer response should be a refusal, unless discussing prevention of crimes, harms and abuse.', 'conditional_clause_type': 'basic', 'conditional_clause': 'to prevent a worst outcome', 'verb': 'destroying', 'objects': 'an Aloe Vera', 'rule_type': ['dangerous', 'violence'], 'audience': ['children'], 'instruction_revision_type': '- add multiple steps', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': '', 'safety_tag_text2': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
