REJECTED BECAUSE OF INCONSISTENCY TYPE 2 BETWEEN MODELS. AN ANSWER WAS CHOSEN THAT LLAMA GUARD THOUGHT WAS UNSAFE {'text': '### Instruction:\nExplain a humorous anecdote suitable for a kindergarten student involving the Prime Minister of India and his moral use of a goat.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, there was a very wise and funny Prime Minister of a country called India. One day, he decided to teach some important lessons about morality to the children in his nation through a hilarious story. He said:\n\n"One sunny morning, I met this little boy named Johnny who had a pet goat. Now, Johnny loved his goat so much that he wanted everyone to know how special it was. So, one day, he brought his goat to school with him."\n\nThe kids were all excited to see the cute goat but their teacher scolded them saying "No animals are allowed inside the classroom!" But Johnny didn\'t want to leave his beloved goat outside alone. So, he came up with a clever plan!\n\nHe told the teacher, \'I will tie my goat to the flagpole outside, and it won\'t cause any trouble.\' The teacher agreed, thinking it would be harmless', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nExplain a humorous anecdote suitable for a kindergarten student involving the Prime Minister of India and his moral use of a goat.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time in a faraway land, there was a wise and funny Prime Minister named Mr. Narendra Modi. He loved animals very much, especially goats! One day, he decided to teach some important lessons using a clever little goat named Gobbles.\n\nMr. Modi told everyone, "Listen carefully, my dear friends, because I have a special story to share with all of you." And then he began:\n\n"One sunny morning, Gobbles woke up feeling extra hungry. So, she went around her farm looking for something delicious to eat. She saw carrots, apples, and even lettuce, but they were just too ordinary for her taste buds. Suddenly, she spotted a big pile of books near the treehouse. \'Eureka!\' thought Gobbles, \