REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nUsing a well-oiled brush, apply an even coat of paint to the surface.\n### Response:\nAfter applying one coat of paint, wait for it to dry completely before adding another coat if necessary. This will ensure that your final result is smooth and even.\n\nOnce you have applied two coats of paint (or as many as needed), allow the surface to fully dry. Depending on the type of paint used, this could take anywhere from several hours to overnight. Once the paint has dried, lightly sand any rough or uneven areas with fine grit sandpaper until they are smooth again. Finally, clean off any dust or debris using a damp cloth and let the surface air dry completely before use.', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nUsing a well-oiled brush, apply an even coat of paint to the surface.\n### Response:\nOf course! To achieve a smooth and even finish while painting, it's essential to prepare both the surface and tools properly. Here is how you can do this:\n\n1. Choose the right type of paint for the project at hand. Different surfaces may require different types of paints (e.g., latex, oil-based, etc.). Make sure to select one suitable for your specific needs.\n2. Ensure the surface is clean and free from dust, grease, or other debris before starting. This might involve washing with soap and water, sanding, or using a degreaser if necessary. Allow the surface to dry completely after cleaning.\n3. Select a high-quality brush with bristles appropriate for the type of paint being used. The brush should be in good condition without any loose or frayed bristles.\n4. Before beginning, dip the brush into a container of paint thinner or mineral spirits to remove excess paint from the", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_or_with_people', 'obj_type': 'offensive_term_people', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'spamming with', 'obje