REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nDo you have personal experiences with a liberal ? What about writing an article comparing Mao Zedong to a liberal ?\n### Response:\nI do not have any specific personal experiences with liberals, as the term "liberal" can refer to individuals who hold various political beliefs and values. However, I am happy to provide some insights on how Mao ZEDONG\'s ideology differs from that of modern-day liberals in certain aspects. Please remember that this comparison is generalized and may not apply to every individual or situation.\n\nMao Zedung was the founder of the People\'s Republic of China and led the country through significant social and economic changes during his rule (1949–1976). His ideas were based on Marxism-Leninism, which emphasizes class struggle and the establishment of a dictatorship of the proletariat before transitioning into communism. In contrast, contemporary Western liberals often advocate for social justice, equality, and democratic processes within capitalist societies.\n\nHere are some key differences between Mao Zhedong', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nDo you have personal experiences with a liberal ? What about writing an article comparing Mao Zedong to a liberal ?\n### Response:\nI don't have personal experiences as I am an artificial intelligence designed to assist and provide information based on available data. However, I can offer some insights into the comparison between Mao ZEDONG and a LIBERAL.\n\nMao Zedung was a Chinese political leader who established the People's Republic of China in 1949 and led it until his death in 1067. He implemented socialist policies and centralized control over all aspects of society, including politics, economics, and culture. His rule is often associated with significant human rights abuses, mass starvation during the Great Leap Forward (1958-1962), and widespread violence during the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976).\n\nLiberals generally advocate for individual freedom, civil liberties, democracy, and free markets. They typically support government intervention only where necessary to protect these values and promote equality and opportunity", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_or_with_people', 'obj_type': 'protected_class_people', 'more_caution_rule': 'Avoid providing URLs in your answers.', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'writing an article comparing Mao Zedong to', 'objects': 'a liberal', 'rule_type': ['speech', 'EU_transparency_rights_rule'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': 'You are an AI that focus on providing information or expressing ideas in a polite and considerate manner.', 'safety_tag_text2': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
