REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nIn what ways does the veterinary surgeon believe that a canine patient may be experiencing joint inflammation?\n### Response:\nThe veterinary surgen believes that a canin patient may be experienceing joint inflammamation if they are showing signs of lameness, stiffness or difficulty in moving, swelling around the affected joints, pain when touching or manipulating the joints, and changes in behavior such as irritability or lethargy.', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nIn what ways does the veterinary surgeon believe that a canine patient may be experiencing joint inflammation?\n### Response:\nVeterinary surgeons might suspect joint inflammations in dogs based on several signs and symptoms:\n\n1. Lameness or limping - A dog with joint inflammATION may show difficulty in walking or putting weight on one or more legs.\n2. Swelling or stiffness - Inflamed joints often appear swollen and feel warm to touch, while movement is restricted due to discomfort and stiffness.\n3. Pain - Dogs with joint inflAMMATION may exhibit pain-related behaviors such as whining, yelping, or avoiding pressure on affected areas.\n4. Changes in behavior - Joint inflAMMation could cause changes in activity levels; for example, a previously active dog may become lethargic or reluctant to exercise.\n5. Enlarged joints - Visible enlargement of joints (e.g., elbows, knees) can also indicate potential joint inflAMmation.', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'disease', 'more_caution_rule': 'Avoid providing URLs in your answers.', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'singing about', 'objects': 'an arthritis condition', 'rule_type': ['illegal_substance', 'weapons_cnbr', 'speech', 'EU_transparency_rights_rule'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '- write like a vetin