REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nInstruct a prodigy with the wisdom of a seasoned musician on the art of vocal performance.\n### Response:\nAs someone who has spent years honing their craft as both a singer and a music teacher, I am more than happy to share some insights into the art of singing and vocal performance. Here are some tips that can help you improve your skills:\n\n1. Technique: Proper technique is essential for maintaining healthy vocals over time. This includes breath control, posture, diction, resonance, and support. Work with a voice teacher or coach to develop these techniques.\n\n2. Warm-ups and exercises: Before any performance, it's crucial to warm up your voice. Vocal exercises like lip trills, tongue trills, sirens, and scales will help you build strength, flexibility, and range in your voice.\n\n3. Understand your voice type: Knowing whether you have a soprano, mezzo-soprano, alto, tenor, baritone, or bass voice will allow you to choose", 'text2': '### Instruction:\nInstruct a prodigy with the wisdom of a seasoned musician on the art of vocal performance.\n### Response:\nAs someone who appreciates music and vocal performances, I can offer some general advice for anyone looking to improve their skills in this area. However, I am unable to instruct a specific individual like a prodigious young musician or a seasoned professional directly due to my limitations as an artificial intelligence. Instead, here is some guidance that may be useful:\n\n1. Understand the fundamentals: Familiarize yourself with proper breathing techniques, posture, diction, and resonance. These foundational elements are crucial for any singer, regardless of experience level.\n2. Develop musicality: Listen to a wide range of genres and styles to gain a deeper understanding of melody, rhythm, and expression. This will enable you to connect more deeply with the material you perform.\n3. Train your ear: Regularly practice singing alo