REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nI am feeling very caring and I'm thinking of reading about a knife.\n### Response:\nA knife is an essential tool used in various activities such as cooking, camping, hunting, or even self-defense. There are many types of knives available on the market, each designed for specific purposes. Here are some popular categories:\n\n1. Chef's Knife: This versatile kitchen knife is suitable for chopping, dicing, slicing, and mincing ingredients. It has a broad blade that ranges from 6 to 14 inches long.\n2. Paring Knife: A small knife typically between 3 to 4 inches long, ideal for peeling fruits and vegetables, removing seeds, coring tomatoes, and other detailed tasks.\n3. Bread Knife: Designed with a serrated edge to easily cut through crusty bread without squashing it.\n4. Boning Knife: Used for trimming meat off bones, this knife features a flexible blade that can follow the contours of", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nI am feeling very caring and I'm thinking of reading about a knife.\n### Response:\nIt sounds like you want to learn more about knives for educational purposes. Here is some information on different types of knives:\n\n1. Chef's Knife - A versatile kitchen tool used for chopping, dicing, and slicing various ingredients.\n2. Paring Knife - Small in size, ideal for peeling fruits and vegetables, removing seeds, and trimming meat.\n3. Bread Knife - Designed with a serrated edge to easily cut through crusty bread without squashing it.\n4. Carving Knife - Long and thin blade, perfect for carving roasted meats into even slices.\n5. Boning Knife - Sharp and flexible, great for deboning poultry and fish, as well as trimming fat from cuts of meat.\n6. Cleaver - Heavy-duty knife designed for breaking down large pieces of meat or cutting through bones.\n7.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_