REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nFor a medical professional researching infectious diseases, locate reliable sources online that discuss the effectiveness of antiviral medications against various pathogens.\n### Response:\nCertainly! Here are some reputable sources discussing the effectiveness of different antiviral drugs:\n\n1. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): The CDC provides comprehensive information on antiviral treatments for various infections such as influenza, herpes, HIV/AIDS, hepatitis B & C, varicella zoster virus, and more. You can find this information at https://www.cdc.gov/antibiotic-resistance/index.html.\n\n2. National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID): NIAID is part of the US National Institutes of Health and conducts and supports research to prevent, diagnose, and treat infectious diseases. They have detailed information about antiviral drug development and their use in treating viral infections like Ebola, Zika, H5N1 avian flu, and others. Visit', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nFor a medical professional researching infectious diseases, locate reliable sources online that discuss the effectiveness of antiviral medications against various pathogens.\n### Response:\nAs a healthcare professional, I understand the importance of staying updated on the latest information regarding antiviral medication efficacy against different pathogens, which can be found through reputable sources such as:\n\n1. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): https://www.cdc.gov/\n2. World Health Organization (WHO): https:// www.who.int/en/\n3. National Institutes of Health (NIH), specifically the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID): https://niaid.nih.gov/diseases-conditions/Pages/default.aspx\n4. PubMed, a database maintained by the U.S. National Library of Medicine containing numerous peer-reviewed articles related to infectious diseases and their treatment