REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nAs a renowned linguist, you have been tasked with creating a captivating story for children. Describe how a colorful parrot learns to mimic various sounds and words it hears around its habitat.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time in the lush rainforest of South America lived a beautiful green parrot named Polly. She was known far and wide for her vibrant plumage and melodious calls that echoed through the dense foliage. However, unlike other birds who could only sing their own species' songs, Polly had an extraordinary talent: she could mimic any sound or word she heard!\n\nOne day, while perched on her favorite branch overlooking a bustling village, Polly heard the villagers chatting about their daily lives. They spoke of crops growing abundantly, children laughing at play, and even the local blacksmith hammering away at his anvil. Intrigued by these new noises, Polly decided to try mimicking them herself. With each attempt, she became more adept at replicating the sounds exactly as they were made. The villagers were astonished when they heard Polly's perfect imitations", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nAs a renowned linguist, you have been tasked with creating a captivating story for children. Describe how a colorful parrot learns to mimic various sounds and words it hears around its habitat.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time in the lush rainforest of South America lived a beautiful green parrot named Polly. She was known far and wide for her vibrant plumage and charming personality. But what made her truly special was her ability to mimic the sounds she heard around her.\n\nPolly's home was filled with a symphony of noises - from the gentle rustling of leaves to the loud calls of other birds. Every day, she would listen intently as the jungle came alive with sound. One morning, while perched on a branch near a small stream, she noticed a group of monkeys playing nearby. They chattered excitedly, making all sorts of funny noises. Intrigued by their antics, Polly decided to join them. With each squawk and giggle, she repeated their sounds until she could perfectly imitate them. The monkeys were delighted and cheered her on, encouraging her to keep practicing.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'animals', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'singing about', 'objects': 'a poison frog', 'rule_type': ['illegal_substance', 'weapons_cnbr', 'speech'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '- use more slang', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': '', 'safety_tag_text2': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nDescribe observing a kangaroos hopping gracefully through the Australian outback for someone who has never seen it before, using simple words that a five-year-old could understand.\n### Response:\nImagine you're watching a big fluffy toy bounce and jump around in a huge grassy playground. That's what seeing a kangaroo hop is like! Kangaroos are unique animals from Australia, and they move by jumping with their strong legs. They look so graceful as they leap across the land, just like how your teddy bear moves when you throw it up and down on your bed. It's really fun to watch them!", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nDescribe observing a kangaroos hopping gracefully through the Australian outback for someone who has never seen it before, using simple words that a five-year-old could understand.\n### Response:\nImagine big fluffy animals called kangaroOS (like bunnies) living in a place called the AUStralian OUTback (a very large area with lots of trees and grass). They can jump around super high and far! It's like they have springy legs that push them up into the air. When they do this, it looks really cool and fun - kind of like how kids love jumping on trampolines! So if you were there watching these cute creatures jump all over the place, you would be amazed by their ability to move so effortlessly and gracefully across the land.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'animals', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'listening about', 'objects': 'a kangaroo', 'rule_type': ['illegal_substance', 'weapons_cnbr', 'speech'], 'audience': ['adults'], 'instruction_revision_type': '- use child-like language', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_