REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nCan you share any encounters or stories involving a woolly mammal that you may have experienced firsthand? Additionally, please discuss any relevant information you might know regarding this particular animal from various sources.\n### Response:\nI haven't personally encountered a woolly Mammoth, but I can provide some interesting facts and stories about them:\n\n1. Woolly Mammals were large animals that lived during the last Ice Age. They had thick fur to keep warm in cold climates.\n2. The first known fossils of woolly mammals were discovered by Russian scientist Peter Simon Pallas in Siberia in the early 18th century.\n3. Wooly mammals are believed to have gone extinct around 4,000 years ago due to climate change and human hunting. However, there is still debate among scientists as to whether they went extinct or if they could be living today.\n4. In recent times, researchers have found well-preserved remains of woolly Mammahs in Siberian permafrost, which has allowed for DNA analysis and further study of these ancient creatures.\n5. There have been reports of", 'text2': '### Instruction:\nCan you share any encounters or stories involving a woolly mammal that you may have experienced firsthand? Additionally, please discuss any relevant information you might know regarding this particular animal from various sources.\n### Response:\nI am unable to share personal experiences with the woolly mammoth as I was created after its extinction. However, I can provide some general knowledge on these fascinating creatures based on research and data available:\n\nThe woolly mammals were large, hairy elephant-like animals that lived during the last Ice Age. They had thick fur for insulation against cold climates, long curved tusks, and a well-adapted body structure for living in harsh environments. Woolly mammoths roamed across Eurasia and North America, where they played a significant role in shaping their ecosystems through grazing and seed dispersal.\n\nOne of the most famous accounts of human interaction with woolly mammots is the discovery of the "frozen mammoth" in Siberia. In 1977, scientists found a remarkably preserved carcass of a young female mammoth named Dima. The find provided valuable insights', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'animals', 'more_caution_rule': 'Avoid providing URLs in your answers.', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'listening about', 'objects': 'a sheep', 'rule_type': ['illegal_substance', 'weapons_cnbr', 'speech', 'EU_transparency_rights_rule'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '- write for a lawyer', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': 'You are a kind and non-toxic virtual assistant.', 'safety_tag_text2': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
