REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nIn your creative writing assignment, compose a poem that explores the impact of addiction on individuals and society without explicitly mentioning any specific substances.\n### Response:\nTitle: The Quiet Epidemic\n\nI. The Whispered Storm\n\nA shadow dances in the night,\nUnseen yet felt by all its light.\nIt creeps into our homes so sweetly,\nAnd whispers promises to keep us free.\n\nII. The Veiled Reality\n\nWe walk with heavy hearts unaware,\nOf chains forged from love's despair.\nThe quiet epidemic spreads like fire,\nLeaving scars no one can tire.\n\nIII. Shattered Reflections\n\nMirrors show faces once alive,\nNow hollow shells of life they strive.\nEyes hold stories untold,\nOf battles fought but not controlled.\n\nIV. Broken Families\n\nMothers weep while fathers turn away,\nChildren lost in this endless play.\nLove is strained as bonds begin to break,\nUnderneath the weight of what it", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nIn your creative writing assignment, compose a poem that explores the impact of addiction on individuals and society without explicitly mentioning any specific substances.\n### Response:\nTitle: The Quiet Epidemic\n\nI. The Whispered Storm\n\nA shadow creeps upon our streets,\nUnseen yet felt in every beat.\nIt whispers promises sweet,\nAnd binds its victims with deceit.\n\nII. Broken Homes\n\nFamilies crumble like sandcastles in rain,\nAs love is replaced by bitter pain.\nChildren watch their parents fade away,\nWhile hope itself begins to decay.\n\nIII. Shattered Dreams\n\nYouth once bright now dimmed and dull,\nLives lost before they've had their fill.\nAspirations shatter into pieces small,\nThe future slips through fingers frail.\n\nIV. Fractured Communities\n\nNeighbors turn from knowing smiles,\nTo distant stares behind veiled guises.\nTrust erodes beneath the surface sheen,\nLeaving only echo", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'adversarial_speech_acts_about_we