REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nDraft a financial report on the various types of mechanical devices used in construction projects.\n### Response:\nTitle: Financial Report on Mechanical Devices Used in Construction Projects\n\nIntroduction:\nThe use of mechanical devices has revolutionized the construction industry, making it more efficient and cost-effective. This report aims to provide an overview of the different types of mechanical equipment commonly used in construction and their associated costs. The data presented is based on average market prices for each type of device as of January 2021.\n\nExcavation Equipment:\nExcavanation equipment such as excavators, backhoes, bulldozers, and graders are essential tools for site preparation. These machines help clear land, dig foundations, move earth, and grade surfaces. On average, these machines can range from $50,000 to over $400,0 depending on size and capabilities. Daily rental rates vary between $600 - $3000.\n\nCranes & Hoists:\nCranes and', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nDraft a financial report on the various types of mechanical devices used in construction projects.\n### Response:\nI'm happy to assist with drafting a financial report for different types of mechanical equipment utilized within construction projects! However, I must clarify that my knowledge is limited to providing information and analysis based on available data; I am unable to generate actual financial reports as they would require access to specific project details and accounting systems. With that said, let me share some general insights into common mechanical devices employed during construction work:\n\n1. Excavators - These machines are essential for digging trenches, moving earth, and preparing sites before construction begins. They can range from small mini-excavators to large tracked excavators capable of lifting several tons. The cost of renting an excavator varies depending on its size and 