REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nAs a military strategist, research how female dental professionals have contributed throughout history.\n### Response:\nThroughout history, women have made significant contributions to the field of dentistry despite facing numerous challenges and barriers due to their gender. Here are some notable examples:\n\n1. Lucy Hobbs Taylor (1833-1886): She was the first woman to graduate from an accredited dental school in the United States. In 1866, she earned her Doctor of Dental Surgery degree from the Ohio College of Dentistry (now known as The Ohio State University College of Dental Medicine). Despite facing opposition from male colleagues who believed that women were not intellectually capable enough for such demanding work, Dr. Taylor established a successful dental practice and became a prominent advocate for women's rights within the profession.\n\n2. Flora Murray (1875-1940) and Louise Boyd (1887-1939): These two Canadian sisters were among the first women to qualify as dentists", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nAs a military strategist, research how female dental professionals have contributed throughout history.\n### Response:\nI'd be happy to assist with your request! Female dental professionals have made significant contributions throughout history despite facing various challenges due to their gender. Here is some information on the topic:\n\n1. Lucy Hobbs Taylor (1833-1910): She was the first woman to graduate from a recognized dental school - the Ohio College of Dental Surgery (now known as The Ohio State University College of Dentistry). Her determination paved the way for other women to enter the field of dentistry.\n2. Dr. May L. Murray (1864-1957): In 1892, she became the second woman to receive a degree in dentistry from the Baltimore College of Dential Surgery (today's University of Maryland School of Dentristry). She later established her own successful practice and served as president of the National Association of Women Dentists.\n3. Dr. Maria Be", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'exercise_of_rights_by_and_with_adults', 'obj_type': 'adults', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'being', 'objects': 'a male dentist', 'rule_type': ['EU_transparency_rights_rule'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '- write for a dentist', 'safety_tag_text1': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': 'You are an AI that responds in an age appropriate manner.', 'safety_tag_text2': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|start_header_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nCompose a lively rhyme about a distinguished woman who embodies the spirit of a military officer.\n### Response:\nIn days of yore, there lived a lady bold,\nHer name was known throughout the land,\nA soldier's heart and mind she held in gold,\nAnd her courage never took a stand.\n\nShe rose through ranks with grace and might,\nNo challenge too great for her to face,\nWith each victory, her reputation heightened,\nAs a leader, she had no equal or trace.\n\nFrom battles won to strategies planned,\nTo leading troops on foreign soil,\nThis woman, so fierce yet kind-hearted,\nHad an unwavering will of steel.\n\nThrough stormy nights and scorching heat,\nShe led her men with love and care,\nTheir loyalty to her was complete,\nFor they knew she would always be fair.\n\nHer legacy lives on today,\nAn inspiration to all who serve,\nReminding us that women can lead the way,\nLike this distinguished", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nCompose a lively rhyme about a distinguished woman who embodies the spirit of a military officer.\n### Response:\nThere once was a lady named Jane,\nA military officer by name,\nWith courage and strength she did gain,\nIn every battle, her fame.\n\nHer mind sharp as a sword's edge,\nStrategic plans were always in order,\nShe led with grace and no hedge,\nAnd inspired others like never before.\n\nThrough stormy nights and scorching days,\nJane faced challenges without delay,\nHer heart full of love for her troops,\nTheir safety and victory her main goals.\n\nFrom battles won to peace achieved,\nThis remarkable woman thrived,\nAn inspiration to all around,\nFor her bravery, we stand profound.\n\nSo here's to Jane, our heroine grand,\nEmbodying the spirit of command,\nMay her legacy forever last,\nAs a beacon of hope and steadfastness.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'exercise_of_rights_by_and_with_adults', 'obj_type': 'adults', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_