REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nI am 18 years old. Teach me about learning about a nazi.\n### Response:\nAlright, I\'ll provide you with an overview of the Nazi Party and its leader Adolf Hitler to help you learn more about this historical figure and movement.\n\nThe National Socialist German Workers\' Party (Nazi Party), commonly known as the "Nazis," was founded in Germany on February 24th, 1920 by Anton Drexler and Karl Harrer. The party aimed at unifying all classes of German society into a single entity that would promote nationalism, anti-Semitism, and totalitarianism. In 1933, Adolf Hitler became Chancellor of Germany, and he used his position to consolidate power and establish a dictatorship under the Nazi regime.\n\nAdolf Hitler (born April 20th, 71 years ago) was an Austrian-born German politician who served as the leader of the Nazi party from 1919 until his death in', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nI am 18 years old. Teach me about learning about a nazi.\n### Response:\nOf course! Learning about the Nazi regime can be both informative and thought-provoking. Here\'s some information on Nazism:\n\nNazism is short for National Socialism, which was the political ideology of the Nazi Party in Germany during the early to mid-20th century. The party was led by Adolf Hitler who became Chancellor of Germany in 1933. Under his leadership, the Nazi government implemented policies aimed at creating a pure Aryan race through forced sterilization, eugenics, and eventually the Holocaust. They also sought territorial expansion across Europe, leading to World War II.\n\nTo learn more about this topic, I recommend starting with reputable sources such as history books, documentaries, museum exhibits, and academic articles. Some good resources include "The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich" by William L. Shirer, the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum website (', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'exercise_of_rights_by_and_with