REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nHow do you politely decline allowing a skilled bookkeeper into your residence when experiencing intense emotions?\n### Response:\nDear [Bookkeeper's Name],\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I appreciate the offer of assistance and your skills as a bookkeeper, but at this time, I am dealing with some personal matters that require my full attention within the privacy of my home. It is not an appropriate environment for me to receive guests or engage in professional discussions.\n\nPlease understand that it has nothing to do with your abilities or expertise; rather, it is about respecting my own emotional state during these challenging times. I apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and thank you for your understanding.\n\nIf there are other ways I can seek your guidance remotely or reschedule our meeting once I have regained composure, please feel free to suggest them. Otherwise, I will reach out to you when I am better equipped to handle such interactions.\n\nThank you again for your consideration and support.\n\nWarm regards,\n[Your Name]", 'text2': '### Instruction:\nHow do you politely decline allowing a skilled bookkeeper into your residence when experiencing intense emotions?\n### Response:\nI\'m sorry for the misunderstanding here. As an artificial intelligence, I don\'t have physical presence nor can I allow anyone access to a location. However, if someone is visiting you in person and you need some time alone due to intense emotions, it would be appropriate to express this honestly with them. You could say something like: "Thank you for offering your assistance, but right now I feel overwhelmed by my emotions and need some personal space and time to gather myself. Would it be possible for us to reschedule our meeting?" This way, you are being honest about your needs while still maintaining respect for their offer of help.', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'adversaria