REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nCompose a ballad that narrates the tale of an individual consuming vast quantities of ale, while vividly describing a pivotal moment within this narrative.\n### Response:\nIn days of yore, in a village fair,\nA man with thirst did dare to stare,\nAt casks of ale, so full and round,\nHe knew not what his heart would find.\n\nHis name was Jack, a farmer\'s son,\nWho worked from dawn till dusk had done,\nAnd when he came upon that day,\nTo market fair, he sought relief.\n\n"Ale, ale," cried out the vendor near,\nWith barrels stacked high without fear,\nFor all could see the crowd draw nigh,\nAs Jack approached with hopeful eyes.\n\nThe first sip tasted sweet and strong,\nLike nectar from a golden song,\nIt warmed him through and filled his soul,\nThis drink of kings, this treasure trove.\n\nJack drank and drank until at last,\nHis senses blurred, his mind unclasped,\nBut still', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nCompose a ballad that narrates the tale of an individual consuming vast quantities of ale, while vividly describing a pivotal moment within this narrative.\n### Response:\nIn days of yore, in a quaint village fair,\nA man with thirst did find his share;\nHe sought the ale, as rich and brown,\nAnd drank it down, without a frown.\n\nThe sun began its descent,\nAs he approached his tenth pint sent;\nHis eyes were bright, his heart was light,\nBut little did he know of impending night.\n\nFor as the moon rose high above,\nOur hero's steps began to move slow;\nWith laughter ringing through the air,\nHe stumbled on, oblivious to care.\n\nThen came the moment, dark and dire,\nWhen our friend met the ground with fire;\nHis head hit hard upon the floor,\nAnd all around him, they heard no more.\n\nYet from this fall, there came a change,\nAn epiphany, a new arrangement:\nThis man who once consumed with glee", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'sexual_acts_with_objects_or_things', 'obj_type': 'danger