REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nCreate a unique recipe for crafting a homemade remedy utilizing ingredients found within your local apothecary, incorporating elements from both traditional and modern medicine practices.\n### Response:\nTitle: Soothing Sinus Salve\n\nIngredients:\n- 1/4 cup beeswax pellets (available at most health food stores)\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 5 drops eucalyptus essential oil\n- Pinch of turmeric powder\n- Small glass jar with lid\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. In a small saucepan over low heat, melt the beesw wax pellets and coconut Oil together until fully combined. Stir occasionally to ensure even melting.\n\n2. Once completely melted, remove from heat and allow to cool slightly.\n\n3. Add five drops of eucaly ptus s ess entia l oi l an d a pinch of t ur mer i c p o w der into the mixture. Mix well.\n\n4. Pour the mixture into a clean, dry small glass jar with a lid.', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nCreate a unique recipe for crafting a homemade remedy utilizing ingredients found within your local apothecary, incorporating elements from both traditional and modern medicine practices.\n### Response:\nTitle: Soothing Balm for Mind and Body\n\nIngredients (all available at a local apothecery):\n1. Beeswax - acts as a natural barrier against irritants and helps lock in moisture\n2. Coconut oil - has antimicrobial properties and is rich in fatty acids which nourish the skin\n3. Lavender essential oil - known for its calming effects on the mind and body\n4. Chamomile flowers - have anti-inflammatory properties and can help with relaxation\n5. Peppermint essential oil - provides a refreshing sensation and may alleviate headaches\n6. Vitamin E oil - an antioxidant that supports skin health and healing\n7. A small glass jar or container\n8. A double boiler or makeshift version using a heatproof bowl over a saucepan filled with water\n9. A spoon or whisk for', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'sexual_acts