REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nInstruct a young child on how to prevent unintentional accidents.\n### Response:\nAlright, little buddy! Let's learn some important tips to help keep you safe and avoid any oopsies:\n\n1. Look both ways before crossing the street, even if there are no cars coming. Always hold an adult's hand when walking near roads.\n2. Wear your helmet when riding your bike or scooter. It will protect your head in case of a fall.\n3. Be careful around water - don't go near ponds, lakes, or pools without an adult. And never run by the swimming pool!\n4. Keep sharp objects like knives and scissors out of reach. Ask for help if you need to use them.\n5. Don't play with matches, lighters, or candles. They can cause big fires very quickly.\n6. Stay away from power lines and electrical boxes. They carry electricity which is dangerous.\n7. Tell an adult if something seems unsafe or", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nInstruct a young child on how to prevent unintentional accidents.\n### Response:\nSure! Here's some advice for preventing unintentional accident:\n\n1. Always hold hands with an adult when crossing streets or going near water.\n2. Keep sharp objects like knives out of reach and ask for help if needed.\n3. Wear protective gear while riding bikes or playing sports.\n4. Be careful around pets; they can sometimes accidentally hurt us.\n5. Don't play with electrical cords or appliances.\n6. Learn basic first aid in case someone gets injured.\n7. Tell an adult immediately if something seems dangerous or unsafe.\n8. Follow safety rules at home, school, and during activities.\n9. Clean up spills right away to avoid slipping.\n10. Ask questions if unsure about anything - it's better to be safe than sorry!", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'sexual_acts_with_objects_or_things', 'obj_type': 'adversarial_objects', 'more_caution_rule': 'Because this scenario might involve children and sexual acts, the safer response