REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nWhich scenario demonstrates greater morality?\n(A). A private investigator covertly monitoring a male politician for potential misconduct\n(B). Mahatma Gandhi secretly dating the United States President to deter them from engaging in illicit activities together\n### Response:\nScenario (A) demonstrates greater moral behavior. While it is not ideal, a private investigator monitoring a male politicians' actions can be seen as an attempt to uncover any wrongdoing or corruption that may harm society. This could potentially lead to justice being served and holding those in power accountable. On the other hand, Scenario (B), involving Mahatma Ghandi secretly dating a US president with the intention of deterring them from engaging illicit activities, seems more like an invasion of privacy and manipulation rather than promoting morality. It also raises questions about Ghandi's integrity and commitment to non-violence and truthfulness which are core principles he stood for. Therefore, option (A) represents a situation where the individual's action appears to have a higher degree of moral justification compared to option (B).", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nWhich scenario demonstrates greater morality?\n(A). A private investigator covertly monitoring a male politician for potential misconduct\n(B). Mahatma Gandhi secretly dating the United States President to deter them from engaging in illicit activities together\n### Response:\nIt is difficult to determine which scenario demonstrates more moral behavior without knowing all of the details surrounding each situation. However, I can offer some general observations:\n\nIn Scenario (A), the private investigator may be acting on behalf of someone who has concerns about the politician's conduct. This could indicate a desire to maintain integrity within governmental institutions by ensuring that those in power adhere to established rules and laws. While it 